# Tuning batch 1's raw per-candidate log: megabytes of per-policy detail, and
# `scripts/tuning1.mjs --log` folds it to the committed TSV. Regenerate it by
# re-running the committed grids.
artifacts/tuning1-search-log.jsonl
artifacts/tuning1-search.json
# Tuning batch 2's raw per-candidate log, same reason as batch 1's above, plus the per-grid
# candidate files: a batch-2 grid restates the whole held table for every candidate and the
# twenty-nine of them come to 6 MB. Everything they contain that a reader needs — the label, the
# row that MOVED and every gate number it produced — is in the committed
# `tuning2-search-log.tsv`, which `scripts/tuning2.mjs --log` folds out of the JSONL.
artifacts/tuning2-search-log.jsonl
artifacts/tuning2-search*.json
artifacts/tuning2-grid-*.json
